                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238668688",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199155260911",
                            "num_reviews": 10,
                            "playtime_forever": 1935,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 411,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1596,
                            "last_played": 1794058536
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "For being one of the few Tokyo Ghoul games out there, this might actually be my personal favorite Tokyo Ghoul game to exist. It sticks pretty well to its original story, and the gameplay and combat are actually not bad! Of course, things can get a little iffy sometimes, and another thing I'd point out is that there aren't that many main story levels since they compressed the game. But that's alright, since the campaign mode offers basically infinite post-game content.\nI'd also say to give the survival game mode a chance, but one thing: DO NOT FIGHT NORO ON HARD DIFFICULTY.\nPutting that aside, the custom character customization is alright (I wish they added more clothing), but it's still good. I think the fact that you can make your own custom ghoul, Quinx, and CCG investigator is sick as hell!\nI also love how they implemented the achievements, so you actually get something like a new quinque or kagune out of them rather than just a basic badge.\nIf you're a Tokyo Ghoul fan, maybe consider playing this game! It can get pretty addicting.",
